////////////////Cinematic - Intro//////////////////
SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli111
"Gimli: What is this place? This rock? I have never seen its like."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn367B
"Aragorn: It was at this Oathstone that the Men of the Mountain swore their false fealty, and sealed their fate."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas120
"Legolas: They have followed us here."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn237
"Aragorn: Oathbreakers, why have you come?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_kod031
"King of the Dead: To fulfil our oath and have peace."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn238
"Aragorn: The hour of doom is now upon us. I will go to Pelargir upon Anduin, and you shall come after me."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn239
"Aragorn: And when this land is clean of the servants of Sauron, I will hold the oath fulfilled, and you shall have peace and depart."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn240
"Aragorn: For I am Elessar, the Heir of Isildur of Gondor."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_elladan049
"Elladan: The wind carries the sounds of battle!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas121
"Legolas: Look ahead! A skirmish!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn370
"Aragorn: Let us hasten to their aid!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli113
"Baruk Khazad!"
End


////////////////Cinematic - Burning Tower 01//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer001
"Pelargir Officer: You have my thanks. But who are you? Why have you come upon Pelargir in its hour of ruin?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn241
"Aragorn: I am Aragorn, son of Arathorn. My companions and I have come to liberate the lands of Gondor."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer002
"Pelargir Officer: My lord... Pelargir burns. The Southrons have come in numbers as yet unseen in our lifetimes."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer003
"Pelargir Officer: They are inside the walls, and guard all passages into the City, by land or by water.\n I fear that soon there will be naught left but smouldering stone."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer004
"Pelargir Officer: We have received word that Angbor of Lamedon is coming, but time is against us\n - and we have no means of entering the City."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn242
"Aragorn: And yet we must. That Gate needs to be opened from within."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer005
"Pelargir Officer: But how?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn267
"Aragorn: I will go."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli112
"Gimli: It is a dangerous task..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn268
"Aragorn: Do not worry, Gimli. I can avoid being seen if I wish."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer006
"Pelargir Officer: We might hasten Angbor's arrival by reclaiming the island of Barad Ciryn.\n The beacon can be seen from afar, and does not burn by day unless catastrophe is upon the City."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn364
"Aragorn: Then I will reclaim it. But first, I need a boat."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer007
"Pelargir Officer: There is an old dock not far from here. But the southrons covet this landing, and will fight to keep it."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer008
"Pelargir Officer: We will need our full strength to reclaim the beach. Let us establish a camp and bolster our forces."
END


//////////////////BEACH//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_elladan047
"This place has been overrun by Corsairs!"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_haldir021
"Sauron has darkened their very hearts!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_elladan064
"These Haradrim are fierce warriors. We must be careful."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer009
"We have taken the dock!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn408
"This vessel will do."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas122
"We will wait for you, until you open the gates."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli129
"Be careful, laddie."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn409
"I must reach the beacon..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirofficer010
"This looks like it was hidden here recently... must've been looted by these raiders."
END

SCRIPT:Hint_Aragorn_Board
"Use the captured fishing boat to transport Aragorn to Barad Ciryn."
END

////////////////LIGHTHOUSE//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_corsair040
"Hark! Who are you, and where'd you come from?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_corsair041
"Oh, aye? I think not. Get him!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_corsair042
"Get over here! We’re getting clobbered!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_bnum029
"Who contests our right of conquest!?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn410
"Your cruelty ends here!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn411
"You should not have entered Gondor!"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn412
"It is done. This should hasten Angbor's forces. Now I must reach the city and make for the gate before we are discovered."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn365
"These tokens are symbols of Umbarian authority. It could come in useful..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn371
"That looks like the safest place to enter the City..."
END

////////////////Cinematic - Dying Guard//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv001
"Dying Guard: They are everywhere... Pelargir has fallen."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn372
"Aragorn: Not yet. Help will come."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv002
"Dying Guard: They are guarding the gate. None can make it out or in."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv006
"Dying Guard: They're stockpiling their infernal firepots. Who knows what they're planning..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn373
"Aragorn: Save your strength."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv003
"Dying Guard: It matters little. Cloaked in black... he appeared from\nthe shadows... and shot me with a poisoned bolt."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv004
"Dying Guard: You... who are you?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pelargirciv005
"Dying Guard: Thank you... my lord."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn397
"Aragorn: Be still."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn398
"Aragorn: That should slow the poison and stem the bleeding.\nStay out of sight until this is over."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn400
"Aragorn: Black cloaks... poisoned darts. The Hasharin have come."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn427x
"Aragorn: They are a dangerous foe... and the streets are teeming with guards.\nI should stay out of sight, lest I bring the whole garrison down upon my head."
END

SCRIPT:hint_hasharin_warning01
"Aragorn must avoid being detected."
END

SCRIPT:hint_hasharin_warning02
"Killing too many guards will alert Hasharin assassins. They must be defeated for Aragorn to remain undetected."
END

SCRIPT:hint_hasharin_warning03
"Hasharin will always detect Aragorn, even when he is stealthed, if he enters their vision."
END

SCRIPT:hint_hasharin_warning04
"While undetected, Aragorn can use these areas to avoid guards."
END


////////////////STEALTH//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn413
